  txt:'In 71 Parkinson\'s brains the substantia nigra was affected in 100% and the nucleus basalis of Meynert in 98.5%. 53% fitted caudo-rostral spread and 47% did not. In 7% the dorsal motor nucleus of the vagus was spared despite nigral and cortical inclusions, so the vagal nucleus is not an obligatory starting point. <sup class="c" data-ref="Kalaitzakis2008" title="Source 167">167</sup>',
