  mech:`Monoclonal antibodies given by infusion bind aggregated alpha-synuclein outside cells, aiming to stop its cell-to-cell spread. <sup class="c" data-ref="Pagano2022,Lang2022" title="Source 186,267">186,267</sup>`,
  txt:`Prasinezumab missed its primary endpoint in PASADENA (316 people) and in PADOVA (586 people; hazard ratio for motor progression 0.84, p=0.066), with a consistent exploratory signal on motor scores. <sup class="c" data-ref="Pagano2022,Nikolcheva2026" title="Source 245,267">245,267</sup> Cinpanemab showed no effect and was discontinued. <sup class="c" data-ref="Lang2022" title="Source 186">186</sup> PADOVA's authors call the subgroup findings "prespecified exploratory" evidence; the sponsor and the publication both frame the phase 3, PARAISO, as the confirmatory test. <sup class="c" data-ref="Nikolcheva2026,Roche2025" title="Source 245,311">245,311</sup>`,
  pt:'Antibodies against synuclein have not yet clearly slowed Parkinson\'s. One gave hints on secondary measures, and a larger trial is now testing it properly.',
